2100	$0<b<1$.  Then the state distance and both complete Pauli-family squared
2101	distances are bounded by
2102	\[
2103	 \delta_{\mathrm{qld}}(16C^2a,b/16,\eps,m,d,q).
2104	\]
2105	Therefore every projective setting in this error range satisfies all three
2106	bounds with $(C_{\mathrm{proj}},b_{\mathrm{proj}})$.  For an arbitrary
2107	strategy of value at least $1-\eps$, questionwise Naimark dilation gives the
2108	same three complete-family conclusions with coefficient
2109	$21C_{\mathrm{proj}}^2$ and power $b_{\mathrm{proj}}$.
2110	\end{theorem}
2111	\begin{proof}
2112	\leanok
2113	Pass from the swap unitaries to their range isometries, absorb the state square
2114	root and the operator factor four, and then apply the Naimark reduction.  The
2115	coefficient $21C_{\mathrm{proj}}^2$ absorbs the completed-family transfer.
2116	\end{proof}
