2118	\begin{theorem}[Explicit raw-effect and qubit soundness]
2119	\label{thm:pauli-soundness-explicit-baseline}
2120	\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.arbitrary_strategy_raw_isometry_bounds_explicit_baseline}
2121	\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_explicit_baseline}
2122	\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_qubit_explicit_baseline}
2123	\leanok
2124	\uses{thm:qld-isometry-baselines-explicit, lem:pauli-edge-card-explicit}
2125	Let $\eps\geq0$ and let an arbitrary strategy for the Pauli basis test have
2126	value at least $1-\eps$.  There are local isometries and one normalized
2127	auxiliary state for which the state distance and both squared distances of the
2128	raw prescribed-answer Pauli effect families are bounded by
2129	\[
2130	 \delta_{\mathrm{qld}}(C_{\mathrm{sound}},b_{\mathrm{sound}},
2131	   \eps,m,d,q).
2132	\]
2133	Here $C_{\mathrm{sound}}\geq1$ and $0<b_{\mathrm{sound}}<1$.
2134	The constant is obtained from the exact raw-effect factor
2135	$2+4\lvert\mathcal E_{\mathrm{Pauli}}\rvert=346$ and the completed-family
2136	coefficient of Theorem~\ref{thm:qld-isometry-baselines-explicit}.  The same
2137	coefficient and power give the qubit-coordinate state and raw operator-family
2138	bounds after the exact field-basis reindexing.  Both conclusions hold on the
2139	full source domain $\eps\geq0$ and introduce no witness hypothesis.
2140	\end{theorem}
2141	\begin{proof}
2142	\leanok
2143	Transfer the completed families to the prescribed raw effects and absorb the
2144	resulting scalar factor into $C_{\mathrm{sound}}$.  For the qubit statement,
2145	reindex the extracted field register along the fixed basis; the state norm and
2146	both operator-family distances are preserved exactly.
2147	\end{proof}
