2166	Let $S$ be a projective Pauli-test setting, let $w$ be a supplied global
2167	polynomial-pair witness, and let $v$ be extraction data with auxiliary vector
2168	$\ket{\mathrm{aux}}$.  For $W\in\{X,Z\}$, write
2169	$D_{\mathrm{swap},\mathrm A}^W$ and
2170	$D_{\mathrm{swap},\mathrm B}^W$ for the squared distances, on the ideal
2171	expanded state determined by this same auxiliary vector, between the
2172	swap-conjugated complete Pauli families and the corresponding ideal Pauli
2173	projectors.  Also put
2174	\[
2175	 s^2=\left\|(V_{\mathrm A}\otimes V_{\mathrm B})\ket{\hat\psi}
2176	   -\ket{\mathrm{aux}}\otimes\ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\otimes M}\right\|^2.
2177	\]
2178	For the local isometries obtained from the actual swap unitaries and EPR
2179	ancillas, the complete Pauli-family distances satisfy
2180	\[
2181	 D_{\mathrm A}^W\leq2D_{\mathrm{swap},\mathrm A}^W+2s^2,
2182	 \qquad
2183	 D_{\mathrm B}^W\leq2D_{\mathrm{swap},\mathrm B}^W+2s^2.
2184	\]
2185	The operators in $D_{\mathrm A}^W$ and $D_{\mathrm B}^W$ are the genuine
2186	isometry conjugates $\phi M_h\phi^\dagger$, with their range projections;
2187	the ideal state is not assumed to lie in either isometry range.
2188	\end{theorem}
